Society. All rights reserved.\n[The Astrophysical Journal](https://iopscience.iop.org/journal/0004-637X),[Volume 892](https://iopscience.iop.org/volume/0004-637X/892),[Number\n2](https://iopscience.iop.org/issue/0004-637X/892/2)**Citation**A. E. McEwen*et al*2020*ApJ***892**76**DOI**10.3847/1538-4357/ab75e2\n\n[PDFOpens in a new tab.](https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.3847/1538-4357/ab75e2/pdf)\n\n[ePub](https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.3847/1538-4357/ab75e2/epub)\n\nYou need an eReader or compatible software to experience[the benefits of the ePub3 file format](http://iopscience.iop.org/page/ePub3).\n\n##\n\nA. E. McEwen\n\nAFFILIATIONS\n\nCenter for Gravitation, Cosmology, and Astrophysics, Department of Physics, University of Wisconsin-Milwaukee, P.O. Box 413, Milwaukee, WI 53201, USA\naemcewen@uwm.edu\n\nEMAIL\n\n[aemcewen@uwm.edu](mailto:aemcewen@uwm.edu)\n\n[https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5481-7559](https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5481-7559)R. Spiewak\n\nAFFILIATIONS\n\nCentre for Astrophysics and Supercomputing, Swinburne University of Technology, P.O. Box 218, Hawthorn, VIC 3122, Australia\n\n[https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6730-3298](https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6730-3298)J. K. Swiggum\n\nAFFILIATIONS\n\nCenter for Gravitation, Cosmology, and Astrophysics, Department of Physics, University of Wisconsin-Milwaukee, P.O. Box 413, Milwaukee, WI 53201, USA\naemcewen@uwm.edu\n\n[https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1075-3837](https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1075-3837)D. L. Kaplan\n\nAFFILIATIONS\n\nCenter for Gravitation, Cosmology, and Astrophysics, Department of Physics, University of Wisconsin-Milwaukee, P.O. Box 413, Milwaukee, WI 53201, USA\naemcewen@uwm.edu\n\n[https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6295-2881](https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6295-2881)W. Fiore\n\nAFFILIATIONS\n\nDepartment of Physics and Astronomy, West Virginia University, Morgantown, WV 26506, USA\n\nCenter for Gravitational Waves and Cosmology, West Virginia University, Chestnut Ridge Research Building, Morgantown, WV 26505, USA\n\n[https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5645-5336](https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5645-5336)G. Y. Agazie\n\nAFFILIATIONS\n\nDepartment of Physics and Astronomy, West Virginia University, Morgantown, WV 26506, USA\n\nCenter for Gravitational Waves and Cosmology, West Virginia University, Chestnut Ridge Research Building, Morgantown, WV 26505, USAH. Blumer\n"}, {"source_id": "source-snapshot:7b6859be459e3021b22a51dce8334ea416b076e1bafb840c03d5235e558232f0", "artifact_id": "artifact:3f42c1ebd4eb6328eb95235320ec525916669e08752a0bb7fc93a3ea4a5dcb66", "sha256": "3f42c1ebd4eb6328eb95235320ec525916669e08752a0bb7fc93a3ea4a5dcb66", "title": "Searching for Technosignatures: Implications of Detection and Non-Detection", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.06550", "locator": {"line_start": 1, "line_end": 179}, "content": "## [1903.06550] Searching for Technosignatures: Implications of Detection and Non-Detection\n\n**Source**: https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.06550\n\n---\n\n[Skip to main content](https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.06550#content)\n\nPress Enter to search ·[Advanced search](https://arxiv.org/search/advanced)\n\n# Astrophysics > Earth and Planetary Astrophysics\n\n**arXiv:1903.06550**(astro-ph)\n\n[Submitted on 14 Mar 2019]\n\n# Title:Searching for Technosignatures: Implications of Detection and Non-Detection\n\nAuthors:[Jacob Haqq-Misra](https://arxiv.org/search/astro-ph?searchtype=author&query=Haqq-Misra,+J),[Anamaria Berea](https://arxiv.org/search/astro-\nph?searchtype=author&query=Berea,+A),[Amedeo Balbi](https://arxiv.org/search/astro-ph?searchtype=author&query=Balbi,+A),[Claudio\nGrimaldi](https://arxiv.org/search/astro-ph?searchtype=author&query=Grimaldi,+C)\n\nView a PDF of the paper titled Searching for Technosignatures: Implications of Detection and Non-Detection, by Jacob Haqq-Misra and 3 other authors[View\nPDF](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1903.06550)Abstract:The search for technosignatures from the Galaxy or the nearby universe raises two main questions: What are the\npossible characteristics of technosignatures? and How can future searches be optimized to enhance the probability of detection? Addressing these questions\nrequires an interdisciplinary approach, combining i) the study of Anthropocene as a planetary transition and thus a possible proxy also for other planets, ii)\nthe active search for technosignatures in the radio/optical and infrared range, and iii) the statistical modelling of technosignatures and Bayesian inference\nmethods to learn from both detection and non-detection. This strategy (combining modelling and observations) offers the best scientific opportunity in the next\ndecade to discover the possible existence of technological civilizations beyond Earth.\n\nComments:Science white paper submitted to the Astro2020 Decadal Survey. arXiv admin note: substantial text overlap\nwith[arXiv:1801.00052](https://arxiv.org/abs/1801.00052)Subjects:Earth and Planetary Astrophysics (astro-ph.EP); Popular Physics (physics.pop-ph)Cite\nas:[arXiv:1903.06550](https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.06550)[astro-ph.EP](or[arXiv:1903.06550v1](https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.06550v1)[astro-ph.EP]for this\nversion)[https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.1903.06550](https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.1903.06550)\n\narXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\n\n## Submission historyFrom: Jacob Haqq-Misra [[view email](https://arxiv.org/show-email/1710b52b/1903.06550)]\n**[v1]**Thu, 14 Mar 2019 03:57:23 UTC (325 KB)\n\n[](https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.06550)Full-text links:\n\n## Access Paper:\n\nView a PDF of the paper titled Searching for Technosignatures: Implications of Detection and Non-Detection, by Jacob Haqq-Misra and 3 other authors\n- [View PDF](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1903.06550)\n\n[view license](http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/)\n\n### Current browse context:\n\nastro-ph.EP\n\n[< prev](https://arxiv.org/prevnext?id=1903.06550&function=prev&context=astro-ph.EP)|[next\n>](https://arxiv.org/prevnext?id=1903.06550&function=next&context=astro-ph.EP)\n\n[new](https://arxiv.org/list/astro-ph.EP/new)|[recent](https://arxiv.org/list/astro-ph.EP/recent)|[2019-03](https://arxiv.org/list/astro-ph.EP/2019-03)\n\nChange to browse by:\n\n[astro-ph](https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.06550?context=astro-ph)\n[physics](https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.06550?context=physics)\n[physics.pop-ph](https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.06550?context=physics.pop-ph)\n\n### References & Citations\n- [NASA ADS](https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/arXiv:1903.06550)\n- [Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?arxiv_id=1903.06550)\n- [Semantic Scholar](https://api.semanticscholar.org/arXiv:1903.06550)\n\nLoading...\n\n## BibTeX formatted citation\n\nloading...\n\nData provided by:[](https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.06550)\n\n### Bookmark[](http://www.bibsonomy.org/BibtexHandler?requTask=upload&url=https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.06550&description=Searching for Technosignatures:\nImplications of Detection and Non-Detection)[](https://reddit.com/submit?url=https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.06550&title=Searching for Technosignatures: Implications\nof Detection and Non-Detection)"}, {"source_id": "source-snapshot:b075e7353865defd102a68e004e70357d4586d20686c1d173746aa005a865b39", "artifact_id": "artifact:ed9c2ae5a563b53b01f5d1748463561d8ce9dd120e9564c7d10a1abb553d5238", "sha256": "ed9c2ae5a563b53b01f5d1748463561d8ce9dd120e9564c7d10a1abb553d5238", "title": "All-sky Ultra-narrowband Spectral Imaging with the OVRO–LWA: Technosignature Constraints and Axion-like Particle Prospects - IOPscience", "url": "https://google.iopscience.iop.org/article/10.3847/1538-3881/ae77f0", "locator": {"line_start": 1, "line_end": 702}, "content": "## All-sky Ultra-narrowband Spectral Imaging with the OVRO–LWA: Technosignature Constraints and Axion-like Particle Prospects - IOPscience\n\n**Source**: https://google.iopscience.iop.org/article/10.3847/1538-3881/ae77f0\n\n---\n\n[](https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.3847/1538-3881/ae77f0)\n\n[](https://iopscience.iop.org/journal/1538-3881)\n\n[The American Astronomical Society (AAS)](https://aas.org/), established in 1899 and based in Washington, DC, is the major organization of professional\nastronomers in North America. Its membership of about 7,000 individuals also includes physicists, mathematicians, geologists, engineers, and others whose\nresearch and educational interests lie within the broad spectrum of subjects comprising contemporary astronomy. The mission of the AAS is to enhance and share\nhumanity's scientific understanding of the universe.\n\nThe following article isOpen access\n\n# All-sky Ultra-narrowband Spectral Imaging with the OVRO–LWA: Technosignature Constraints and Axion-like Particle Prospects\n\nNikita Kosogorov,Gregg Hallinan,Greg Hellbourg,Marin M. Anderson,Judd D. Bowman,Ruby Byrne,Morgan Catha,Bin Chen,Xingyao Chen,Sherry Chhabra\n\nPublished 2026 June 24•© 2026. The Author(s). Published by the American Astronomical Society.\n[The Astronomical Journal](https://iopscience.iop.org/journal/1538-3881),[Volume 172](https://iopscience.iop.org/volume/1538-3881/172),[Number\n1](https://iopscience.iop.org/issue/1538-3881/172/1)**Citation**Nikita Kosogorov*et al*2026*AJ***172**44**DOI**10.3847/1538-3881/ae77f0\n\n[PDFOpens in a new tab.](https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.3847/1538-3881/ae77f0/pdf)\n\n[ePub](https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.3847/1538-3881/ae77f0/epub)\n\nYou need an eReader or compatible software to experience[the benefits of the ePub3 file format](http://iopscience.iop.org/page/ePub3).\n\n##\n\nNikita Kosogorov\n\nAFFILIATIONS\n\nCahill Center for Astronomy and Astrophysics, California Institute of Technology, Pasadena, CA 91125, USA; nakosogorov@gmail.com, nkosogor@caltech.edu\n\nOwens Valley Radio Observatory, California Institute of Technology, Big Pine, CA 93513, USA\n\nEMAIL\n\n[nakosogorov@gmail.com](mailto:nakosogorov@gmail.com)\n\n[nkosogor@caltech.edu](mailto:nkosogor@caltech.edu)\n\n[https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1226-118X](https://orcid.org/0000-0003-12