ers/1903.06550)|[Disable MathJax](javascript:setMathjaxCookie())([What is MathJax?](https://info.arxiv.org/help/mathjax.html))", "error": null, "created_at": "2026-08-13T19:23:28.361328+00:00"}, {"id": "tool-receipt:863b48e1e799141b31699c0d", "attempt_id": "attempt:807d733238d21d47e53fad6c", "server": "anysearch", "tool": "extract", "arguments": {"url": "https://google.iopscience.iop.org/article/10.3847/1538-3881/ae77f0"}, "result": "## All-sky Ultra-narrowband Spectral Imaging with the OVRO–LWA: Technosignature Constraints and Axion-like Particle Prospects - IOPscience\n\n**Source**: https://google.iopscience.iop.org/article/10.3847/1538-3881/ae77f0\n\n---\n\n[](https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.3847/1538-3881/ae77f0)\n\n[](https://iopscience.iop.org/journal/1538-3881)\n\n[The American Astronomical Society (AAS)](https://aas.org/), established in 1899 and based in Washington, DC, is the major organization of professional astronomers in North America. Its membership of about 7,000 individuals also includes physicists, mathematicians, geologists, engineers, and others whose research and educational interests lie within the broad spectrum of subjects comprising contemporary astronomy. The mission of the AAS is to enhance and share humanity's scientific understanding of the universe.\n\nThe following article isOpen access\n\n# All-sky Ultra-narrowband Spectral Imaging with the OVRO–LWA: Technosignature Constraints and Axion-like Particle Prospects\n\nNikita Kosogorov,Gregg Hallinan,Greg Hellbourg,Marin M. Anderson,Judd D. Bowman,Ruby Byrne,Morgan Catha,Bin Chen,Xingyao Chen,Sherry Chhabra\n\nPublished 2026 June 24•© 2026. The Author(s). Published by the American Astronomical Society.\n[The Astronomical Journal](https://iopscience.iop.org/journal/1538-3881),[Volume 172](https://iopscience.iop.org/volume/1538-3881/172),[Number 1](https://iopscience.iop.org/issue/1538-3881/172/1)**Citation**Nikita Kosogorov*et al*2026*AJ***172**44**DOI**10.3847/1538-3881/ae77f0\n\n[PDFOpens in a new tab.](https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.3847/1538-3881/ae77f0/pdf)\n\n[ePub](https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.3847/1538-3881/ae77f0/epub)\n\nYou need an eReader or compatible software to experience[the benefits of the ePub3 file format](http://iopscience.iop.org/page/ePub3).\n\n## \n\nNikita Kosogorov\n\nAFFILIATIONS\n\nCahill Center for Astronomy and Astrophysics, California Institute of Technology, Pasadena, CA 91125, USA; nakosogorov@gmail.com, nkosogor@caltech.edu\n\nOwens Valley Radio Observatory, California Institute of Technology, Big Pine, CA 93513, USA\n\nEMAIL\n\n[nakosogorov@gmail.com](mailto:nakosogorov@gmail.com)\n\n[nkosogor@caltech.edu](mailto:nkosogor@caltech.edu)\n\n[https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1226-118X](https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1226-118X)Gregg Hallinan\n\nAFFILIATIONS\n\nCahill Center for Astronomy and Astrophysics, California Institute of Technology, Pasadena, CA 91125, USA; nakosogorov@gmail.com, nkosogor@caltech.edu\n\nOwens Valley Radio Observatory, California Institute of Technology, Big Pine, CA 93513, USA\n\n[https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7083-4049](https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7083-4049)Greg Hellbourg\n\nAFFILIATIONS\n\nCahill Center for Astronomy and Astrophysics, California Institute of Technology, Pasadena, CA 91125, USA; nakosogorov@gmail.com, nkosogor@caltech.edu\n\nOwens Valley Radio Observatory, California Institute of Technology, Big Pine, CA 93513, USA\n\n[https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8191-3885](https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8191-3885)Marin M. Anderson\n\nAFFILIATIONS\n\nOwens Valley Radio Observatory, California Institute of Technology, Big Pine, CA 93513, USA\n\nJet Propulsion Laboratory, California Institute of Technology, Pasadena, CA 91011, USA\n\n[https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2238-2698](https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2238-2698)Judd D. Bowman\n\nAFFILIATIONS\n\nSchool of Earth and Space Exploration, Arizona State University, Tempe, AZ 85287, USA\n\n[https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8475-2036](https://orcid.org/00